<title>BOTSWANA: Standard Chartered half yr shr doubles.</title>
<headline>Standard Chartered half yr shr doubles.</headline>
<dateline>GABORONE 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>		    (million pula unless stated)</p>
<p>    Eps (thebe)		   160.2     vs   82.2</p>
<p>    Div (thebe)		    42.5     vs   20.4</p>
<p>    After tax			23.062   vs   11.840</p>
<p>    Net income		     56.764   vs   44.660</p>
<p>    Net interest income	  36.760   vs   28.432</p>
<p>    Other operating income     20.004   vs   16.228</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge    0.727   vs    2.953</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			  30.749   vs   15.376</p>
<p>    Tax				 7.687   vs    3.536</p>
<p>Full name: Standard Chartered Bank Botswana Limited</p>
<p>Div payable: August 1</p>
<p>On register: July 23</p>
<p>NOTE -The bank said its latest results underlined its sound performance following restructuring undertaken in 1995/96.</p>
<p>The capital adequacy position of the Bank remained strong with a ratio of more than 20 percent against a requirement of eight percent under the Banking Act.</p>
<p>It said it was well positioned to cope with the improving economy in Botswana and the lending opportunities that this might present.</p>
<p>-- Gaborone newsroom +267 347182</p>
</text>
